<section id="faqs"><h2>Frequently asked: Excavation &amp; Site Prep in Lower Mainland</h2><h3>What does basement excavation cost in Vancouver?</h3><p>$45 to $75 per cubic yard for standard residential. Add $15 to $25 for rock, hard-pan, or contaminated soil disposal.</p>
<h3>Do I need an environmental permit?</h3><p>For sites within 30 metres of a stream, yes — DFO and provincial environmental approvals add 4 to 8 weeks to the timeline.</p>
<h3>How big a machine do I need for a 2,500 sq ft basement?</h3><p>Mid-size 8 to 12 tonne excavator runs the dig. Mini-ex (3 tonne) handles trenching and finish work.</p>
<h3>What about soil disposal?</h3><p>Class 1 (clean) disposal runs $35 to $55 per cubic yard. Contaminated soil clears $180 plus, with lab testing required.</p>
<h3>Why an excavators.tv exclusive partner?</h3><p>One licensed excavation contractor per metro. Generals avoid the unlicensed-bobcat race and book the verified shop with WorkSafeBC clearance.</p>
<h3>Can you handle shoring and underpinning?</h3><p>Engineered shoring requires P.Eng stamp. Territory partners pre-qualify with structural engineers so the shoring drawings drop in 2 weeks not 8.</p></section>


